     {
      "text": "Abbijam -- Called Abijah, 2 Chronicles 13:1."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 14,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "high places -- Cf. 2 Chronicles 14:3. It appears that local sacrifices to Jehovah (though not according to the divine order) were offered in the times of the kings upon \"high places\" (cf) 1 Samuel 9:12. Apparently Asa's mother had defiled one of these with an idol, 1 Kings 15:13. Asa destroyed the idol and the idolatrous (but not the Jehovistic) \"high places.\" But see \"high places,\" (See Scofield \"1 Kings 3:2\")."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 24,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Jehoshaphat -- Called Josaphat, Matthew 1:8."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
